{
  "status": "fixed",
  "summary": "Added a 'Set current as default' button to the Appearance settings (so the user's chosen colors become the Reset-to-defaults target, persisted to localStorage), plus a command-prompt-inspired color-scheme picker with 7 presets.",
  "prTitle": "Add 'set as default' button and color-scheme presets to settings",
  "prBody": "## What & why\n\nResolves #2. The Appearance panel let you customize note/label colors but only offered a hard-coded \"Reset to defaults\". This adds the two things the issue asked for:\n\n1. **\"Set current as default\" button** — saves your current colors as *your* defaults (stored in `localStorage` under `pt-theme-default`). \"Reset to defaults\" now returns to those saved defaults, falling back to the factory palette if you've never set one.\n2. **Color-scheme picker** — a dropdown of command-prompt-inspired presets: Classic Green (DOS), Amber (CRT), Matrix, PowerShell Blue, Ubuntu Terminal, Solarized Dark, and Command Prompt. Selecting one applies its palette live; editing a color afterward flips the dropdown back to \"Custom…\".\n\n## Implementation notes\n- `js/app.js`: introduced `THEME_SCHEMES` (preset palettes) and a `themeDefaults` layer with `saveDefaults()`; the active `theme` now initializes from last-used colors (`pt-theme`) then user defaults then factory. Wired up the scheme `<select>` (populated from `THEME_SCHEMES`), the `setDefaultTheme` button, and updated the reset handler.\n- `index.html`: added the scheme select and the \"Set current as default\" button to the Appearance panel.\n- No CSS changes needed — reused existing `.panel`/`.wide`/`.crow` styles.\n\n## Testing\n- `node --check js/app.js` passes.\n- Pure additive change to existing client-side theme logic; no server or dependency changes.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n- Confirm the preset colors read well against the dark stage background; tweak hex values in `THEME_SCHEMES` if any feel off.\n- Behavior: change a color → \"Set current as default\" → change again → \"Reset to defaults\" should return to the saved default, not the factory one.",
  "comment": ""
}
